"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/96625-official-vampire-resources-faq-bloodlines-lexicon-animal-stats-index </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Here are some official resources for Vampire: The Requiem, up to date for Blood and Smoke. Documents Lexicon (https://docs.google.com/spreadsheet/ccc?key=0ArFqVit </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T07:16:01-07:00","id":485388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485382#post485382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The link for the new bloodlines, as well as other Requiem 2e stuff, found here.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/96625-official-vampire-resources-faq-bloodlines-lexicon-animal-stats-index\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...al-stats-index</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for that!<br /> <br /> Looked at the information, and it is certainly an interesting new take on them, and their signature Discipline. Well worth a read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T07:32:34-07:00","id":485394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485388#post485388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you for that!<br /> <br /> Looked at the information, and it is certainly an interesting new take on them, and their signature Discipline. Well worth a read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are official 2e versions. Not fan-made. Hopefully there will be a book with them before too long.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:05:13-07:00","id":485470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485394#post485394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are official 2e versions. Not fan-made. Hopefully there will be a book with them before too long.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Had another look at it. I'm not happy with the idea that they are Strix beatsticks, but then, I'm not a big fan of the Strix. They were really interesting in Requiem for Rome, but after that, they get worse and worse, as the idea is seized upon, taking them from being the reason one of the Clans was created (and destroyed,) to one that hates vampires, but is secretly trying to become them as well. It starts to muddy the waters of the idea that each Clan has a separate origin and creation. If it wee a case that they were haunting the Ventrue, saying to them that they are the children of their fruits, that they are the founders of their clans... then you have something interesting right there, and something that works. Are they <i>really</i> the creators, or just saying it for their own goals? And if they are lying... what are their reasons for doing so? If they are telling the truth, why emerge now? And what are they wanting from the Ventrue... and can they afford to refuse any demands from them?<br /> <br /> But enough of my issues with the Strix... The Khaibit have an extra layer to them now. If you have other monsters and supernatural threats in the City, then they might be able to fight them off. They then have a <i>purpose</i> for existing, and that would strengthen the bloodline.This is something they lacked in the original write-up, a sense of direction and purpose. And they make sense as bodyguards and protectors, and I feel there is a huge amount that can be done with them, untapped potential. How do they recruit their childer? Is it just an Embrace, or is there a period of training, moulding and shaping their minds and bodies to fulfill the potential their would-be Sires saw in them originally? Maybe she is just an average looking, plain office worker who is in a dead end, and not really going anywhere... but if she is taken, Ghouled and made to exercise and train... after a year she is a honed weapon, her mind looking at everyone as a potential threat, assessing the people around. Are they threats? Are they unwitting hindrances to the mission her Sire-to-be gave her? If she fails, would he punish her... and how? Spending the night in an bathtub filled with ice cubes, whilst reciting a mantra over and over, having to ignore the freezing temperature? Or maybe it is something else, more... inhuman? And after her years of training is over, and she realises she is nothing like the plain office worker she once was, does she look in horror at what she has become... or does she feel pride and accomplishment, and pleasure that her Mentor saw the spark of potential in her, and he saw fit to turn it into a fire?<br /> <br /> So much is there, and what we have is just the tip of the iceberg. Some bloodlines are only really going to need ten or so pages to flesh them out. The Khaibit are a bloodline that could have an entire book dedicated to them, and you would find that there were still plenty of questions to ask after reading it. I suspect this is why they are so popular, and one of my favourite things from Requiem.<br /> <br /> Then there is Obtenebration... It goes int &quot;hunt the Strix&quot; mode a bit, and we all know by now what my sentiments on them are by now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That said, you can rework them to get rid of those elements... and they have cracked the nut. If you look back to VTM, and see the Lasombra's version, you see that it was something that could be deeply frightening and powerful... but was quite clunky. V20 has improved it quite a bit... but you end up feeling that there is something missing from the equation. They have found the answer, and have given a brilliant framework. Why only five Devotion powers, though? There could be lots more! Like turning a person's shadow into a spy, going around and gathering information on those being observed... as an example.<br /> <br /> In short, there is a lot given to us, but also a lot more potential unrealised.<br /> <br /> Just my take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:20:12-07:00","id":485514,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, there is no discussion of any special fixation on the Ventrue by the Strix in 2nd Edition. Have you read their section of the 2e Requiem core?<br /> <br /> Both their chapter and the Storyteller's section do a lot to give you a better idea of the role that Strix serve within the narrative of the Kindred and of a Vampire: The Requiem game. It's quite good and a stronger presentation than that given in <i>Night Horrors</i>, I feel. (No offense to the Night Horrors writers, I think they just benefited a lot from 2e refinement!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:39:25-07:00","id":485522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485470#post485470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had another look at it. I'm not happy with the idea that they are Strix beatsticks, but then, I'm not a big fan of the Strix. They were really interesting in Requiem for Rome, but after that, they get worse and worse, as the idea is seized upon, taking them from being the reason one of the Clans was created (and destroyed,) to one that hates vampires, but is secretly trying to become them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their relationship with vampires is a bit more complicated than that. They don't &quot;want to be&quot; vampires, they believe that vampires are just like them, but with physical bodies of their own. And yet, the vampires deny this fact. Instead of indulging in all the debaucheries afforded by physical form, they just act as much like regular humans as possible. That's why the Strix hate them, for being a waste of potential. They're The Joker, they want to prove that deep down everyone (or every vampire, anyway) is just one bad day away from being just as monstrous as they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485470#post485470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It starts to muddy the waters of the idea that each Clan has a separate origin and creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the Clan entries in 2e? They pretty much straight up confirm that not only do the clans have different origins, but there are most likely multiple origins within each individual clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485470#post485470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it wee a case that they were haunting the Ventrue, saying to them that they are the children of their fruits, that they are the founders of their clans...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why the Ventrue? The Ventrue are not the Julii, the Strix have no special connection to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485470#post485470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then you have something interesting right there, and something that works. Are they <i>really</i> the creators, or just saying it for their own goals? And if they are lying... what are their reasons for doing so? If they are telling the truth, why emerge now? And what are they wanting from the Ventrue... and can they afford to refuse any demands from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from the Ventrue-specific part, this is exactly how the Strix are presented in 2e. Some of them claim to be the origin of all vampires. Some only claim to be the origin (and end) of the Julii. Some make no such claims whatsoever. Why the lies? Why the contradictions? What do they want? Why are they disturbingly vampire-like in some ways and completely different in others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:40:45-07:00","id":485669,"title":"","content":"Just as a reminder, I did end my post with &quot;Just my take on it.&quot; I'm not expecting people to agree with any part of what I said - I know that the vast majority won't. Nor did I say that what I was saying was canon.<br /> <br /> I also need to apologise, because it seems I failed to make clear that I was trying to show how - in my perspective - the Strix would have made sense. I also seemed to have failed to make clear that there is no certain claim (in my scenario) that the Ventrue and the Julii are the same clan. But then... where did the Ventrue come from? And they clearly came <i>after</i> the Roman period, because there is no record of them in the year 543 AC/CE, because they are not in the Byzantium appendix in Fall of the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> More importantly, this is no longer on the topic that this thread was started under... is there another thread all of this could be discussed in? I don't want to be the instigator of a thread derailment... I am putting up this reply, and am leaving it at that, intending to stick to the Khaibit and Obtenebration after this point. Any further discussion - in the right thread - I would be happy to continue with. Or by PM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485522#post485522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their relationship with vampires is a bit more complicated than that. They don't &quot;want to be&quot; vampires, they believe that vampires are just like them, but with physical bodies of their own. And yet, the vampires deny this fact. Instead of indulging in all the debaucheries afforded by physical form, they just act as much like regular humans as possible. That's why the Strix hate them, for being a waste of potential. They're The Joker, they want to prove that deep down everyone (or every vampire, anyway) is just one bad day away from being just as monstrous as they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right... if vampires are just like them, then it lends very strongly to the notion that <i>all</i> clans originate in some form from the Strix. They can merge with a body, or a vampire, and take control. They also in the process become a vampire themselves, and one of the five clans. If they were becoming Clanless, or part of some Strix-orientated clan, I could understand... but it seems rather confused, to me. But if everyone else sees sense in it, that's fine. I'm not trying to dictate what is - or is not - canon here. In any case, I ended up waiting for this to come out, because it was a month or so behind schedule. So I ended up creating my own version of the Strix, and they are nothing like what Onyx Path have created. So this is all an academic exercise for me, because the setting I'm still building up is very different to what was originally presented by OPP. Again, if everyone else loves the Strix, think they are great, I'm happy for them. I don't like them, and have something that works, which was an evolution on the original snippets and tidbits I could get hold of. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you read the Clan entries in 2e? They pretty much straight up confirm that not only do the clans have different origins, but there are most likely multiple origins within each individual clan. </div> </div> </div>Just re-read them. It's been a while. Don't get me started on Akhenaten... that one is a load of rubbish. Interesting how they keep on using fairy tales to explain the origins, at least possible interpretations and possibilities. Point of interest, one of the Ventrue origins state they are the last scions of the Camarilla... page twenty seven. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why the Ventrue? The Ventrue are not the Julii, the Strix have no special connection to them. </div> </div> </div>Can you prove this? Can you hold this as absolute fact? That the Strix have no special connection to the Ventrue? As already mentioned, the Ventrue are the youngest Clan, and a source of mystery on that front. Who is to say that the Strix didn't try their experiment again?<br /> <br /> In any case, I said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Are they </i><i>really</i><i> the creators, or just saying it for their own goals? And if they are lying... what are their reasons for doing so? If they are telling the truth, why emerge now? And what are they wanting from the Ventrue... and can they afford to refuse any demands from them?</i> </div> </div> </div>I never said that the Strix - <b>in my scenario</b> - were connected with the creation. I said that the Strix <i>claimed</i> that they were. Then went into possibilities to be being true, and false. My scenarion is not canon, and I claim not that it is.<br /> <br /> And what do we have with the Strix and the Julii? An origin myth that suggests that the Strix turned a Revenant into a full vampire. Again, look at the Ventrue, and then the Julii. If they are not the same, then why are they so startlingly similar? The Discipline spread, clan weakness... It has always been hinted and teased at that the two might well be intertwined, if not an evolution of the clan... And we are again at the question: Where did the Ventrue come from? But, again, this is going beyond the scope of the thread, which is meant to be about the Khaibit and Obtenebration. I have no issue with discussing it further, but... I again ask, is there another thread this can be transferred to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apart from the Ventrue-specific part, this is exactly how the Strix are presented in 2e. Some of them claim to be the origin of all vampires. Some only claim to be the origin (and end) of the Julii. Some make no such claims whatsoever. Why the lies? Why the contradictions? What do they want? Why are they disturbingly vampire-like in some ways and completely different in others? </div> </div> </div>Um... because Rose Bailey and the development team wanted it that way? Seriously, you seem to not understand that the intention is to make us come up with answers, and to then have the adventures we want to have. The thing is, we can make the Strix into whatever we want. Do they need to just harass vampires? Why not werewolves? What if they suddenly turn up, and claim they are the source of their creation, not Father Wolf? Not saying it should happen, but someone out there will likely have come up with that idea, and run it - and the group enjoyed the plot twists it presented.<br /> <br /> I did buy and read this back when it was Blood and Smoke, for the record. And I went through the Strix chapter carefully, because I had no choice. I had been playtesting a version of the nWoD, and was seeing if what I had put together worked. In any case, people had seen my development notes for playable characters (they had asked to understand the characters better), and had seen a bit about the Strix in one of them. About how they were using a girl to hunt vampires, making her do it. She was gaining power and protection whilst doing it, if I recall correctly. I got questions about all of that, and I had to admit it had been an idea I had put in there, but had forgotten about. I had said that I wasn't going that direction any more, and I got asked why, and in the end I had to have them. They proved popular, and something of a hit. I had turned that original adventure into a novel by that time, so I added them in, to explore them. I still am, building up the game universe by writing stories. And they appear, in the background... and I still have no definitive answer to them. But what I ended up with is cool and brilliant, and something I know will be a hit when I get to start running the setting.<br /> <br /> And I think that is what it is all about, to be fair. We can split hairs about the little details, but we all need to follow the directions we feel compelled to, and if we have fun in the process, then we are doing things right.<br /> <br /> And I still think the Khaibit are cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:21:48-07:00","id":485709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485669#post485669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right... if vampires are just like them, then it lends very strongly to the notion that <i>all</i> clans originate in some form from the Strix. They can merge with a body, or a vampire, and take control. They also in the process become a vampire themselves, and one of the five clans. If they were becoming Clanless, or part of some Strix-orientated clan, I could understand... but it seems rather confused, to me. </div> </div> </div> </div>Just as a point of clarification, it says in the Strix section that when they use Synthesis on a mortal or a revenant, that's when it creates one of the Kindred, but the Clan of that Kindred tends to be determined by that of the last Kindred said Strix possessed. Which adds to the confusion on whether the Strix preceded the clans or vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:38:53-07:00","id":485722,"title":"","content":"It also says that if there's no such connection it's randomly determined. So it could be that the clans are based on quirks of the people originally synthesised. Nowadays it's practically impossible for there not to be some connection to an existing clan somewhere so you don't get any new ones popping up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:42:46-07:00","id":485728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=32598#post32598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thanks for the info. Since I havr Bloodlines: The Hidden already, I am all set it seems. I just wondered if there was an update, that's all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the second edition version of the KHaibit.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Shadow and the Asp &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T18:00:45-07:00","id":485870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485669#post485669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right... if vampires are just like them, then it lends very strongly to the notion that <i>all</i> clans originate in some form from the Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assumes a monolithic vision of what the Strix are that doesn't scan. &quot;Strix&quot; is like &quot;Kindred&quot; \u2014 it's not a term for only one kind of being, and the Strix are as mutable as Blood-based vampires (if not moreso) besides.<br /> <br /> The Jiang Shi of the Triangle have been getting more like Kindred vampires across the generations \u2014 what does that say about the strain of vampirism they represent and its relation to humanity?<br /> <br /> The Strix gain Vitae in a completely different fashion from how corporeal vampires gain it and vent their Supernatural Tolerance Trait in a viscerally different manner to how the Kindred lose Blood Potency \u2014 what does that say about the Blood?<br /> <br /> &quot;<a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/83024157855/they-say-there-are-many-unique-curses-theres\" target=\"_blank\">There are many unique curses</a>&quot; has been an element of VtR since at least the 1e clanbooks. The Strix's occasional claim to be the source of the Beast or the Beast itself has evidence to support it and examples that contradict it, because they are only one supercategory of vectors for the Curse.<br /> <br /> It could be that early Nosferatu rose from improper burials because the Strix were attracted by the inauspiciousness of a soul not put to rest, but it could also be that some squirming thing from within the earth seized an opportunity instead. It could be that the Daeva were raised from the ground by the passions of the dead for the living, or maybe some Owls puked blood down their gullets.<br /> <br /> The thing about vampires \u2014 of every stripe \u2014 is that <i>they lie all the time.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T21:21:13-07:00","id":486013,"title":"","content":"Coming from someone who wasn't particularly enticed by Requiem 1e, and thus missed out on the fluff: am I the only one believing the Requiem 2e story elements, at this point, would benefit a lot from a &quot;for dummies&quot; introduction? :P<br /> <br /> I'm mining as much as I can from the Requiem 2e Rulebook and Vampire Translation guide, in order to understand what &quot;meta-plot&quot; is implied behind all the &quot;Storyteller's discretion&quot;. I'd like to know, basically, what is the &quot;story so far&quot;. I know I sound like a VTM guy with paradigm change issues, but a lot of the &quot;unreliable narrator&quot; origin stories are not easy for me to piece together as a prospective Storyteller trying to see what I want to utilize in my own game.<br /> <br /> To be clearer:<br /> <br /> Is there a timeline of events that explains all this stuff in a comprehensive fashion? Something that links the clan's origins, the Strix, and other supernaturals into a &quot;minimalist&quot; arch-mythos?<br /> <br /> I'd, for example, love to understand the Mekhet and Khaibit more, what with their obvious Egyptian naming and origin stories, I'd like to understand where Dracula (thus Ordo Dracul) fits in all this, understand the Fall of the Camarilla and the Longinus myth, etc.<br /> <br /> Where can I get my One Myth to Rule them All and Bind Them ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T21:39:36-07:00","id":486016,"title":"","content":"There's no one myth. There's a different origin for each clan, and even each clan could have different origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T21:50:32-07:00","id":486020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=486013#post486013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I get my One Myth to Rule them All and Bind Them ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is no metaplot save the barest concessions like &quot;New Orleans was hit by Hurricane Katrina a couple years after the 1e corebook featuring it as a signature setting was published&quot; and the PC vampires are implied verging on outright stated to be a bunch of different kinds of creatures with a common grounding in their conditions being inflicted upon a human base, which itself seems to have a unifying/stabilizing influence on their supernatural qualities as the Blood pools and runs together over time.<br /> <br /> The 1e clanbooks cover a lot of ground in describing the five mainline clans throughout history, bearing in mind that the Ventrue book is told largely from the perspective of someone whose elder contact is explicitly told by said contact not to trust a word he says because memory-alteration is one of the clan's stocks in trade and the Mekhet book spends a good deal of narrative space underlining the difference between the truth and what one reader has termed &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?464972-V-tR-Unravelling-the-Clanbooks-(Warning-very-long-and-spolierish!)&amp;p=11359594#post11359594\" target=\"_blank\">History told not to inform the listener, but to manipulate.</a>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-20-2015, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T21:54:31-07:00","id":486021,"title":"","content":"OH, okay Barbe, I think I get what you're coming from.<br /> <br /> On Clan origins, it's important to look at the origins of the Clans as basically being irrelevant. <i>Requiem </i>isn't overly concerned with progenitors and a genealogy of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all the history that <i>Requiem </i>2e seems concerned with can be found in a few key places, namely <i>Requiem for Rome</i> and <i>Dark Eras: Requiem for Regina. </i>Those give you the history that's most definitely &quot;still canon.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want <i>more </i>history that <i>may or may not still be canon</i> then you should look at <i>Ancient Mysteries</i>, which has several time periods and different locations.<br /> <br /> For the Khaibit, you want to look at <i>Bloodlines: The Hidden</i>. The trick of reading their write up is to keep in mind that the blog post supercedes that writeup. If you read it though, you can really clearly see where they cleaned it up and focused it.<br /> <br /> For most Second Edition stuff, they don't reference things from 1e without sort of re-explaining them in the context of the new edition. I think <i>Dark Eras </i>is the only exception sort of, because it references some material from the first edition Lancea Sanctum book?<br /> <br /> If you have any other questions, feel free to PM me or we could start a new topic to lay it out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T23:20:17-07:00","id":486044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix?p=485322#post485322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for this. I've only just seen you post, because I've only just started to use the forum again, now I have a computer with an up-to-date browser that can view it...<br /> <br /> I don't have the Clanbooks, but if I get hold of the Mekhet one, I'll look Felix up. He clearly is of interest: Why was he spared, when his siblings disappeared? And what happened to his Sire?<br /> <br /> Questions, questions...</div> </div> </div> </div>From what can be guessed colating the bits from Fall of the Camarilla and the clanbooks, Felix was &quot;adopted&quot; by a major Daeva elder in Constantinople by the time of his true sire's destruction, resulting in his actual origins as Mekhet being forgotten through the ages and it is partly implied that, initially, Felix had no idea the Khaibit and their myths were for real and though his sire was just a crazy paranoid elder and killed for it - not exactly surprising, considering it was obsessed with a supernatural threat no one else seemed to understand or even perceive and imposing orders based upon this. Obviously, Felix learned better through the ages, developed Obtenebration on his own spontaneously and will track down clues of the Owls in the periods between torpors, from time to time re-starting anew as the &quot;Daeva childe&quot; of someone whose memories he rewove through Dominate, more or less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-09-2016, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T00:05:35-07:00","id":486061,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Prince Maxwell of Chicago commit diablerie on his spymaster, Norris, when Norris found out he had attempted to steal Ordo Dracul secrets to get around his thirst for vampire blood as he reached 6 Blood Potency and confronted him about it. Maxwell was meeting with a mage who was going to force the secrets from a Dragon at the time. Prince Maxwell basically came forward to the court about it, told them they'd just have to live with it, because every other option was horrible. He also befriended Bruise Miner, the tormented nosferatu, after propping him up as a sort of figurehead for the Carthians and humiliating Solomon Birch. I believe Maxwell is risking Bruise's current lack of ambition to drink from him, hoping he won't attempt to abuse the Vinculum.<br /> <br /> Solomon Birch and Persephone Moore, meanwhile, have begun colluding together.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, Olivia Citysmith may have gone complete Bale Hound and recruited her packmate Thomas to the job, she may be on the move with the help of Piggy and others. In the Rockies, Moriarty of the Black Moon eXtreme was, after another vampire hunt gone wrong, approached by a spirit attempting to recruit him to the Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> Apparently some stuff has happened in Mage.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But aside from that and a couple other things, there isn't really metaplot, which refers to an advancing story. There is just setting and background. A lot of it is unclear, and a lot of the stuff that seems clear may be untrustworthy because for thousands of years there have been forces great and small just flat out lying about things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2015, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T01:27:10-07:00","id":486112,"title":"","content":"It's less a metaplot and more a series of retcons though. <br /> <br /> Like the strix coming back. That's not something that happened <i>between </i>first edition and second. They've <i>always </i>been back now. In fact in places it sounds like they never went away at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}